<title>USA: Wachovia to buy Florida bank for $222 million.</title>
<headline>Wachovia to buy Florida bank for $222 million.</headline>
<dateline>WINSTON-SALEM, N.C. 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wachovia Corp. said on Thursday it reached a definitive agreement to acquire 1st United Bancorp, a Boca Raton, Fla., commercial bank, in a stock swap valued at $222 million.</p>
<p>Wachovia said the agreement has been approved by the boards of both companies, but is still subject to approval of 1st United's shareholders and by regulators. It expects the merger to close by year-end.</p>
</text>
